WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.204
Shrink a PDF to fit an email limit.

2
00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:08.093
Gmail, Outlook and upload forms all have size caps.

3
00:00:08.093 --> 00:00:13.010
A practical routine to get under them: find the heavy part, pick the right

4
00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:15.136
preset, and split when you must.

5
00:00:16.536 --> 00:00:18.779
Know your limit, then leave headroom.

6
00:00:18.779 --> 00:00:21.144
The common limits are easy to remember.

7
00:00:22.444 --> 00:00:25.350
Step 2: compress with the right preset.

8
00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:27.585
Compress PDF has four presets.

9
00:00:28.885 --> 00:00:33.259
Step 4: split when you must. Sometimes a document is just big.

10
00:00:34.559 --> 00:00:39.245
A word on cloud links. For really large files, the honest answer is often

11
00:00:39.245 --> 00:00:41.300
a link instead of an attachment.

12
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:45.582
To try it, open Compress PDF in OpenFile.

13
00:00:45.582 --> 00:00:49.728
Drop in a file, adjust the settings and press the button.

14
00:00:49.728 --> 00:00:53.437
It all runs on your device, so nothing is uploaded.

15
00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:59.647
Read the full post, with live demos, on the OpenFile blog.
